    /begin CHARACTERISTIC 
      /* Name                   */      CLCOke_b_DisableClutchReqFromNotAppliedWhenNotAvailable 
      /* Long Identifier        */      "Selects if disabling of clutch requst die to not GearAvailable shall be done when in a not applied state (i.e. not InGear/Torque/Disengage) or only not be allowed from Neutral.
      
      Set to true to prevent new request (i.e. set to Neutral) when previous request wasn't applied.
      Set to false to prevent new request (i.e. set to Neutral) when previous request is Neutral.
      
      Will only have affect if the Disable time is set to a enabled value.
      When triggered, will require extrernal request to go to Neutral before accepting New request even if Gear becomes available
      "
      /* Type                   */      VALUE 
      /* ECU Address            */      0x0000 /* @ECU_Address@CLCOke_b_DisableClutchReqFromNotAppliedWhenNotAvailable@ */ 
      /* Record Layout          */      Scalar_BOOLEAN 
      /* Maximum Difference     */      0 
      /* Conversion Method      */      CM_T_BOOLEAN 
      /* Lower Limit            */      0.0 
      /* Upper Limit            */      1.0
      EXTENDED_LIMITS
      /* Extended Lower Limit   */      0.0
      /* Extended Upper Limit   */      1.0
    /end CHARACTERISTIC
    
